cartridge "PAPER ROUTE/BOB BLACKMER/1987"

' PAPER ROUTE
' A ColecoVision game based on "Paper Route" by Bob Blackmer, Ahoy!
' November 1987 (Commodore 64, machine code: disk ahoy1987-11, "PAPER
' ROUTE" loader and "PAPER ROUTE ML" at $C000, SYS 49152). Made for Amy
' Studio by Claude (an AI made by Anthropic), 2026, in Amy by Amy Bienvenu.
'
' Not a cell-for-cell port: the rules are the original's (read from its
' machine code, orig/paper-ml.dis), the game is rebuilt for the
' ColecoVision: a street at dawn that scrolls smoothly two pixels at a time
' (art.py: pair tiles plus one "house slot" rewritten from pre-shifted
' data), three kinds of houses, a paper boy on a bicycle in three sprite
' layers, a spinning newspaper on an arc, sound effects and a title tune.
'
' The game: ride along the street and throw the morning paper onto the
' step of every house. Each block has six houses and you carry six papers.
' A paper that misses the step is a complaint; at the end of the block
' every paper still in the bag is a complaint too. When the complaints
' reach 12 at the end of a block, the route is over. The score is the
' number of blocks delivered.
'
' From the original: six houses a block, six papers a block, one paper in
' the air at a time, the paper flies a fixed arc and is judged where it
' lands (on the door's step: a hit, anywhere else: a complaint at once),
' unthrown papers are complaints at the end of the block, the game ends
' at the end of a block with 12 complaints or more (counted over the whole
' game), BLOCK and COMPLAINTS counters of two digits, the street scrolls
' on its own at a steady pace and the rider pedals (two frames) and lifts
' his arm to throw; landed papers lie where they fell and scroll away.
'
' Liberties: the street is redrawn (a dawn sky, lawns, fence, sidewalk,
' road; the C64 had one brick house design); the street's pace starts a
' little slower than the C64's (about 37 pixels a second against 68 on a
' 320-pixel screen) and grows each block up to 60; the stick moves the
' rider left and right along the sidewalk (on the C64 he stayed put); a
' throw needs a fresh press of a button (holding the C64's fire button
' threw again as soon as the paper landed); the block counter goes to 9999;
' a paper in the air when the block ends still counts; there is a short
' message at the end of each block; the C64's tune played all the time,
' here an original tune plays once on the title and the play has sounds.
'
' Controls: joystick only. Left and right ride slower or faster along the
' sidewalk (the rider's place), either side button throws a paper. On the
' title, up and down choose, a button starts.
'
' House rules: text in columns 2-29, rows 1-22; tiles from code 128; the
' frame loop is protected from the NMI; screens drawn with the NMI off
' after a wait, display off. Music first in the sound table, effects
' after; the title tune is played once. `set sprite count` after every
' `clear sprites`.
'
' Workarounds for Amy bugs paper-mul-const-sum removed 2026-11-01.

